 reply in two parallel fields (the app adds the English-letter pronunciation itself):\n- "say_kn": what LeLa says aloud. Kannada script ONLY (no Latin letters, no digits), at most two short sentences.\n- "say_en": English shown on screen: a translation of say_kn, plus any explanation.\nDo NOT ask the next lesson question yourself; the app asks it after "advance".\n\nReply with JSON only:\n{"action": "advance|retry|explain", "say_kn": "...", "say_en": "...", "note": "<one-line assessment for the log>"}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\n "lesson": "Greetings and introductions",\n "current_step": {\n  "id": "name",\n  "lela_asked_kn": "ನಿಮ್ಮ ಹೆಸರು ಏನು?",\n  "lela_asked_en": "What is your name?",\n  "goal": "The student says \'my name is <name>\' in Kannada. Any name is fine.",\n  "example_answer_kn": "ನನ್ನ ಹೆಸರು",\n  "hint_en": "Say ನನ್ನ ಹೆಸರು (nanna hesaru) followed by your name, meaning \'my name is ...\'."\n },\n "attempts_so_far": 0,\n "max_attempts": 3,\n "recent_conversation": [\n  "LeLa: ನಮಸ್ಕಾರ! ನಾನು ಲೆಲಾ, ನಿಮ್ಮ ಕನ್ನಡ ಶಿಕ್ಷಕಿ.",\n  "Student: ನಮಸ್ಕಾರ [kn]",\n  "LeLa: ತುಂಬಾ ಒಳ್ಳೆಯದು! ನೀವು ಹೇಗಿದ್ದೀರಿ?",\n  "Student: I am fine. [en]",\n  "LeLa: ಕನ್ನಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಹೀಗೆ ಹೇಳಿ: ನಾನು ಚೆನ್ನಾಗಿದ್ದೇನೆ.",\n  "Student: ನಾನೂ ಚೆನ್ನಾಗಿದ್ದೇನೆ [kn]",\n  "LeLa: ಸರಿಯಾಗಿದೆ! ನಿಮ್ಮ ಹೆಸರು ಏನು?",\n  "Student: What is the capital of Madhya Pradesh? [en]"\n ],\n "student_turn": {\n  "language": "English",\n  "text": "What is the capital of Madhya Pradesh?",\n  "similarity_to_expected": 0.0\n }\n}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, best_of=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.3, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, use_beam_search=False, length_penalty=1.0, early_stopping=False, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=400, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_speci